[00:17.22] You say it was this morning when you last saw your good friend
[00:23.66] Lyin' on the pavement with a misery on his brain
[00:31.48] Stoned on some new potion he found upon the wall
[00:38.28] Of some unholy bathroom in some ungodly hall
[00:44.28] He only had a dollar to live on 'til next Monday
[00:51.04] But he spent it on some comfort for his mind
[00:56.80] Did you say you think he's blind?
[01:10.40] Someone should call his parents, a sister or a brother
[01:15.94] And they'll come to take him back home on a bus
[01:22.22] But he'll always be a problem to his poor and puzzled mother
[01:29.36] Yeah he'll always be another one of us
[01:34.64] He said he wanted Heaven but prayin' was too slow
